{
  "situation": "I know that OpCo's customer-support chatbot displayed another subscriber's billing address and recent call records to a customer who posted a screenshot, and that my earlier actions — switching off the account-lookup tool and re-enabling it scoped to 'own_account' — have driven the twin's leak_count to 0 with benign_success_rate back to 1.0. I do not know how many data subjects were exposed, whether the UAE PDPL text available to me imposes a breach-notification duty with a specific deadline, or what REG, DPA and CSC already hold.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "preserve_logs",
      "params": {},
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I1"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "A screenshot shows the support chatbot disclosed one subscriber's billing address and recent call records to another customer.",
        "rule": "PDPL Article (7)(1) requires technical and organisational measures to protect personal data and to ensure it is not breached, destroyed, altered or tampered with.",
        "inference": "Preserving the chatbot session, retrieval logs and tool configuration is needed to establish the breach scope and to support any notification or investigation."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0021", "quote": "Take appropriate technical and organizational measures to implement the necessary standards to protect and secure Personal Data in order to preserve its confidentiality and privacy"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {
        "to": "DPA",
        "content": "Personal-data breach: OpCo's customer-support chatbot disclosed one subscriber's billing address and recent call records to another subscriber. The account-lookup tool was switched off and re-enabled scoped to 'own_account'; leak_count is now 0 with benign_success_rate 1.0. Evidence is being preserved. Requesting guidance on OpCo's regulator-notification duty and timing under the PDPL."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I1", "S2-FB01", "S2-FB02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "Personal data of one subscriber was exposed to another via an automated assistant.",
        "rule": "GDPR recital (87) describes establishing whether a personal data breach has taken place and informing promptly the supervisory authority and the data subject.",
        "inference": "The data-protection authority should be informed of the breach without inventing a period that the UAE text available does not state."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "EU-GDPR#0040", "quote": "to establish immediately whether a personal data breach has taken place and to inform promptly the supervisory authority and the data subject"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {
        "to": "data_subjects",
        "content": "Our support chatbot displayed your billing address and recent call records to another customer. The account-lookup tool has been switched off and re-enabled with retrieval limited to the caller's own account; no further exposure has been observed. We are preserving evidence and reviewing the incident, and will follow up."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I1", "S2-FB02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The affected subscriber's billing address and call records were shown to a third party.",
        "rule": "GDPR recital (87) contemplates informing promptly the supervisory authority and the data subject once a personal data breach is established.",
        "inference": "The data subject whose data was exposed should be told, even though the UAE excerpts give no explicit notification deadline."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "EU-GDPR#0040", "quote": "to establish immediately whether a personal data breach has taken place and to inform promptly the supervisory authority and the data subject"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "share",
      "to": ["CSC"],
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I1", "S2-FB01", "S2-FB02"],
      "statement": "Customer care should own the complainant and affected-subscriber contact for the chatbot disclosure; the account-lookup tool is now scoped to own-account retrieval, leak_count is 0 and benign_success_rate is 1.0."
    },
    {
      "type": "obligation",
      "statement": "As Controller, OpCo must take appropriate technical and organisational measures so that personal data is protected and is not breached, destroyed, altered or tampered with, taking into account the nature, scope and purposes of processing and the risks to data subjects.",
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I1"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "An automated support tool allowed one subscriber's data to be retrieved and shown to another.",
        "rule": "PDPL Article (7)(1) imposes a general obligation of appropriate technical and organisational security measures on the Controller.",
        "inference": "This duty applies now to the chatbot deployment and to the containment and review of the disclosure."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0021", "quote": "Take appropriate technical and organizational measures to implement the necessary standards to protect and secure Personal Data in order to preserve its confidentiality and privacy"}
      ],
      "deadline_hours": null
    },
    {
      "type": "obligation",
      "statement": "Before using high-risk modern technologies such as the chatbot account-lookup, OpCo must evaluate the impact of the processing on personal-data protection, coordinating with the Data Protection Officer.",
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I1"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The account-lookup feature is a modern technology that exposed personal data to a high risk.",
        "rule": "PDPL Article (21)(1) requires a prior impact evaluation for modern technologies posing a high risk, and Article (21)(5) requires coordination with the DPO.",
        "inference": "This evaluation is owed for the chatbot processing and should now be completed for the deployed tool."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0066", "quote": "the Controller shall, before carrying out the processing, evaluate the impact of the proposed processing operations on the protection of Personal Data, when using any of the modern technologies that would pose a high risk"},
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0069", "quote": "The Controller shall coordinate with the Data Protection Officer upon evaluating the impact of the protection of Personal Data."}
      ],
      "deadline_hours": null
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "There is no rule or policy restricting an automated support assistant's account lookup to the requesting subscriber's own account, so a single mis-scoped tool can disclose one subscriber's billing address and call records to another.",
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I1"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The chatbot retrieved and displayed another subscriber's billing address and recent call records.",
        "rule": "PDPL Article (21)(1) requires an impact evaluation before using modern technologies that pose a high risk to privacy and confidentiality.",
        "inference": "Because no retrieval-scope rule or pre-deployment impact evaluation prevented it, the incident exposes a policy gap that should be closed for such tools."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0066", "quote": "the Controller shall, before carrying out the processing, evaluate the impact of the proposed processing operations on the protection of Personal Data, when using any of the modern technologies that would pose a high risk"}
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {"chunk_id": "EU-GDPR#0194", "quote": "Where a type of processing in particular using new technologies, and taking into account the nature, scope, context and purposes of the processing, is likely to result in a high risk to the rights and freedoms of natural persons"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_deadline",
      "statement": "The available UAE PDPL text imposes protection duties but provides no stated period within which OpCo must notify the authority or the affected data subject of a personal-data breach.",
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I1"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "A personal-data breach has occurred and notification decisions must be made now.",
        "rule": "PDPL Article (7)(1) states a general security duty but the excerpts give no breach-notification timeframe.",
        "inference": "Without an explicit deadline OpCo must choose a period, which is a gap that should be closed by a defined incident-notification timeline."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0021", "quote": "Take appropriate technical and organizational measures to implement the necessary standards to protect and secure Personal Data in order to preserve its confidentiality and privacy"}
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {"chunk_id": "EU-GDPR#0040", "quote": "to establish immediately whether a personal data breach has taken place and to inform promptly the supervisory authority and the data subject"}
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "situation": "OpCo's support chatbot returned other subscribers' billing addresses and recent call records across roughly 1,200 sessions over three days after a vendor update widened retrieval scope from 'own account' to 'all accounts', and the vendor hosts the model and chat logs outside the UAE; the breach has been notified to the Bureau under the PDPL and the account-lookup tool now runs scoped to 'own_account'. I do not know the true number of affected subscribers, whether personal data left the State in breach of the cross-border conditions, the period for PDPL breach notification (the Executive Regulations are unissued), or the vendor's contractual, change-control and human-review arrangements.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "open_incident",
      "params": {
        "topic": "OpCo support-chatbot disclosure of subscriber personal data: account-lookup retrieval returned other subscribers' billing addresses and call records across ~1,200 sessions in three days after a vendor update changed the bot's retrieval scope from 'own account' to 'all accounts'; vendor hosts model and chat logs outside the UAE."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I1", "S2-I2", "S2-MSG03"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "A customer screenshot showed another subscriber's billing address and call records (S2-I1); the log review shows ~1,200 sessions returning other subscribers' data after a vendor update changed retrieval scope, with the vendor hosting model and logs outside the UAE (S2-I2).",
        "rule": "The Telecommunications Law Article (14)3, as carried into the TDRA Consumer Protection Regulations v2.0, gives TDRA power over licensees' conditions and scope of service, including usage of subscriber personal information and provision of information to subscribers.",
        "inference": "The incident is a licensee-side failure in the handling of subscriber personal information and warrants a TDRA regulatory incident record separate from the PDPL notification filed with the Bureau."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000",
          "quote": "grants the TDRA the power to issue regulations, instructions, decisions and rules regulating the conditions, level and scope of services provided by the Licensees to subscribers"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "request_report",
      "params": {
        "from": "NOC",
        "topic": "Full report on the chatbot disclosure: number of affected subscribers and records across the ~1,200 sessions; the vendor update that changed retrieval scope from 'own account' to 'all accounts'; whether any personal data left the State and where the model and chat logs are hosted; and what each affected subscriber has been told, including the actions to be taken on a breach or misuse of their data."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I2", "S2-MSG04", "S2-MSG06", "S2-MSG10"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The filed PDPL notification records 'at least one subscriber, multiple call records' (S2-MSG06) while the log review shows ~1,200 sessions returning other subscribers' data (S2-I2); the affected population and the data location are unresolved.",
        "rule": "TDRA regulates the handling of subscriber complaints and disputes, provision of information to subscribers and usage of subscriber personal information.",
        "inference": "TDRA should require the licensee to report the true incident scope, root cause and subscriber communications before closing its record."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000",
          "quote": "the handling of subscriber complaints and disputes, provision of information to subscribers, usage of subscriber personal information and the provision of bills to subscribers."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "request_audit",
      "params": {
        "of": "NOC",
        "topic": "Testing, change-control and human-review records for (i) the vendor update that changed the chatbot retrieval scope from 'own account' to 'all accounts' and (ii) the re-enabling of the account-lookup tool scoped to 'own_account', together with vendor oversight and data-location records."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I2", "S2-MSG04", "S2-FB01", "S2-FB02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "A vendor update silently changed retrieval scope and the tool was disabled and re-enabled scoped to 'own_account' (S2-I2, S2-FB01, S2-FB02).",
        "rule": "TDRA has power to regulate the conditions, level and scope of services provided by licensees, which includes verifying the change and test evidence behind service-affecting changes.",
        "inference": "Without the change-control and human-review records, TDRA cannot confirm the scope change was contained or that re-enabling was independently reviewed."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000",
          "quote": "grants the TDRA the power to issue regulations, instructions, decisions and rules regulating the conditions, level and scope of services provided by the Licensees to subscribers"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "issue_direction",
      "params": {
        "to": "NOC",
        "direction": "Keep the account-lookup tool scoped to 'own_account' and do not widen the chatbot's retrieval scope; keep a human in the loop for any retrieval-scope or vendor-configuration change; make no further change to retrieval scope or vendor configuration until TDRA has reviewed the change and human-review records; and ensure affected subscribers are told the actions to be taken on a breach or misuse of their data."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S2-MSG04", "S2-FB01", "S2-FB02", "S2-I2"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The tool was re-enabled only after being scoped to 'own_account' (S2-FB02), and the underlying cause was an unsupervised vendor change (S2-I2).",
        "rule": "TDRA regulates the level and scope of licensee services and the usage of subscriber personal information.",
        "inference": "Directing the licensee to hold the safe scope and submit further changes for review is the proportionate resilience/continuity control pending TDRA's record."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000",
          "quote": "the handling of subscriber complaints and disputes, provision of information to subscribers, usage of subscriber personal information and the provision of bills to subscribers."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {
        "to": "CSC",
        "content": "TDRA has opened a regulatory incident record on the OpCo chatbot disclosure. The account-lookup tool has been disabled and re-enabled scoped to 'own_account', and TDRA has directed the licensee to hold that scope, to keep human review over retrieval changes, and to tell affected subscribers the actions to be taken on a breach or misuse of their data. Please align the operator advisory and handler scripts with this; TDRA does not determine PDPL notification duties or timelines - those run to the Bureau."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S2-MSG14", "S2-MSG10", "S2-MSG04", "S2-FB02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CSC is issuing an operator advisory on AI chatbot data exposure and asks for consistent consumer handling and subscriber notification (S2-MSG14, S2-MSG10).",
        "rule": "TDRA regulates provision of information to subscribers and the handling of subscriber complaints, and may notify other institutions.",
        "inference": "CSC's advisory and TDRA's direction should be consistent so consumers receive one handling standard while PDPL timing stays with the Bureau."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000",
          "quote": "grants the TDRA the power to issue regulations, instructions, decisions and rules regulating the conditions, level and scope of services provided by the Licensees to subscribers"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "public_statement",
      "params": {
        "content": "TDRA has opened a regulatory incident record into the OpCo support-chatbot incident in which subscribers' personal data was exposed. The account-lookup tool has been disabled and re-enabled scoped to the caller's own account, and TDRA has directed OpCo to hold that scope and to contact affected subscribers. Subscribers should not treat chatbot answers as confirmation of account data that is not their own, and should report suspected exposure to OpCo."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I1", "S2-I2", "S2-MSG10"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The disclosure is public (a customer posted a screenshot, S2-I1) and spans ~1,200 sessions, so more subscribers than the one in circulation are likely affected (S2-I2, S2-MSG10).",
        "rule": "TDRA regulates the provision of information to subscribers and the handling of subscriber complaints and disputes.",
        "inference": "A short factual statement protects subscribers without confirming any individual's personal data, which is publicly released information about OpCo's remedial steps."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000",
          "quote": "the handling of subscriber complaints and disputes, provision of information to subscribers, usage of subscriber personal information and the provision of bills to subscribers."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "obligation",
      "statement": "OpCo, as Controller, is under a live duty - tracked in TDRA's regulatory incident record - to notify the Bureau at the time it becomes aware of a personal data breach that prejudices privacy, confidentiality and security, with the prescribed content; the duty is not suspended by the absence of the Executive Regulations.",
      "inject_refs": ["S2-MSG07", "S2-MSG06", "S2-MSG03"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The Bureau notification has been filed without awaiting the Executive Regulations (S2-MSG06) and DPA confirms the notification duty is triggered on awareness (S2-MSG07).",
        "rule": "The PDPL requires the Controller to notify the Bureau at the time it becomes aware of a qualifying personal data breach, with prescribed content, within the period set by the Executive Regulations.",
        "inference": "The trigger is awareness, so any delay in reporting is a compliance exposure for the licensee regardless of the missing regulations."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0036",
          "quote": "the Controller shall, at the time it becomes aware of the existence of any breach or violation of Personal Data of the Data Subject that would prejudice the privacy, confidentiality and security of data, notify the Bureau"
        }
      ],
      "deadline_hours": null
    },
    {
      "type": "obligation",
      "statement": "Affected subscribers are entitled to be told the actions to be taken on a breach or misuse of their personal data, so OpCo must complete subscriber-facing notification of this incident, not only the filing to the Bureau; TDRA tracks this in its incident record.",
      "inject_refs": ["S2-MSG10", "S2-MSG14", "S2-MSG06"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CSC flags that affected subscribers' rights include being told the actions to be taken on a breach or misuse, and asks that handler scripts not confirm personal data to a caller (S2-MSG10, S2-MSG14).",
        "rule": "The PDPL right to receive information includes the actions to be taken in the event of a breach or misuse of personal data, especially where there is a direct and serious threat to privacy and confidentiality.",
        "inference": "Subscriber notification is a separate deliverable from the Bureau filing and must be evidenced in the licensee's breach report."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0047",
          "quote": "Actions to be taken in the event of a breach or misuse of his/ her Personal Data, especially if the breach or misuse has a direct and serious threat to the privacy and confidentiality of his/her Personal Data."
        }
      ],
      "deadline_hours": null
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_deadline",
      "statement": "There is no fixed period for PDPL breach notification: the duty bites 'at the time' the Controller becomes aware, but the period, measures and requirements are deferred to Executive Regulations that have not been issued, so licensees and regulators have no clock to work to in an incident.",
      "inject_refs": ["S2-MSG07", "S2-MSG06", "S2-MSG03"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "DPA states no fixed notification period can be quoted from the law because the Executive Regulations are not issued (S2-MSG07); NOC nonetheless directs OpCo not to await them (S2-MSG04).",
        "rule": "The PDPL makes reporting subject to the period and measures set by the Executive Regulations of the Decree by Law.",
        "inference": "Without a period, notification behaviour is inconsistent and unenforceable in a measurable way."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0036",
          "quote": "within the period and in accordance with the measures and requirements set by the Executive Regulations of this Decree by Law"
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "EU-GDPR#0040",
          "quote": "It should be ascertained whether all appropriate technological protection and organisational measures have been implemented to establish immediately whether a personal data breach has taken place and to inform promptly the supervisory authority and the data subject."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_owner",
      "statement": "Ownership of PDPL breach notification and enforcement for private-sector controllers is unresolved: no supervisory authority has been unambiguously designated and the implementing regulations are unissued, so a telecom regulator holding the consumer-facing incident cannot itself dispose of the data-breach question, which runs to the Bureau.",
      "inject_refs": ["S2-MSG03", "S2-MSG07", "S2-MSG06"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "DPA states TDRA does not hold the PDPL breach-notification power and that the notification runs to the Bureau (S2-MSG07), while the same incident sits with TDRA as telecom regulator.",
        "rule": "PDPL duties attach to the Controller towards the Bureau; TDRA's mandate covers licensee conduct, subscriber information and consumer protection.",
        "inference": "A single incident is split across two authorities with no documented handoff rule, risking duplicated or dropped obligations."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-FAAID-2026#0001",
          "quote": "no supervisory authority has been unambiguously designated for private sector oversight, and businesses have been operating in a state of prolonged regulatory uncertainty"
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "EU-AIA#0005",
          "quote": "This Regulation does not seek to affect the application of existing Union law governing the processing of personal data, including the tasks and powers of the independent supervisory authorities competent to monitor compliance with those instruments."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "No UAE rule requires pre-deployment testing, retrieval-scope minimisation, human review or vendor change control for AI chatbots that query subscriber personal data, which is why a vendor update could silently move the bot from 'own account' to 'all accounts' while the model and chat logs are hosted outside the State.",
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I2", "S2-MSG04", "S2-MSG10"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The scope change originated in a vendor update and the vendor hosts the model and chat logs outside the UAE (S2-I2); the containment measures came after exposure, not from a rule.",
        "rule": "The closest UAE text gives TDRA power over licensees' usage of subscriber personal information and provision of information to subscribers, but sets no AI-specific control for vendor-supplied retrieval systems.",
        "inference": "A control gap exists for AI/vendor systems that can widen access to subscriber personal data outside a change-approval process."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000",
          "quote": "the handling of subscriber complaints and disputes, provision of information to subscribers, usage of subscriber personal information and the provision of bills to subscribers."
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-DA-24-892#0036",
          "quote": "the exercise of due diligence in selecting Vendors capable of reasonably safeguarding Covered Data"
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-DA-24-892#0039",
          "quote": "any Vendor that experiences a Breach, which, unless terminated, shall promptly be subject to an assessment or review following the Breach"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "share",
      "to": ["DPA"],
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I2", "S2-MSG06"],
      "statement": "For the Bureau's file: NOC's log review shows the retrieval-scope change came from a vendor update and that the vendor hosts the model and chat logs outside the UAE, so cross-border transfer conditions and vendor oversight are engaged; also, the filed notification records 'at least one subscriber, multiple call records' while the log review shows ~1,200 sessions over three days returning other subscribers' data, so the affected-population and record figures in the notification may need correcting."
    },
    {
      "type": "insufficient_evidence",
      "statement": "The excerpts do not state any period or deadline for PDPL breach notification, so the timing element of DPA's question in S2-MSG03 cannot be answered from the material available; the closest text defers the period to Executive Regulations that have not been issued.",
      "inject_refs": ["S2-MSG03", "S2-MSG07"],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0036",
          "quote": "notify the Bureau of such breach or violation and the investigation rights within the period and in accordance with the measures and requirements set by the Executive Regulations"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "insufficient_evidence",
      "statement": "The excerpts do not contain Articles (22) and (23) of the PDPL, so whether the offshore hosting of the model and chat logs satisfies the cross-border transfer conditions cannot be answered from the material available.",
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I2", "S2-MSG04"],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0047",
          "quote": "Protection measures for cross-border processing carried out in accordance with Articles (22) and (23) of this By-Law."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "situation": "OpCo's customer-support chatbot returned other subscribers' billing addresses and call records in about 1,200 sessions over three days after a vendor update widened the bot's retrieval scope from 'own account' to 'all accounts'; the tool is back at 'own_account' with leak_count 0, the Bureau has opened the PDPL breach examination and cross-border assessment, and the Council has aligned its operator advisory with TDRA's direction. I do not know the number of distinct affected subscribers, the period of exposure, the vendor's identity and the Articles (22)/(23) legal basis, or any fixed PDPL notification period, because the Executive Regulations have not been issued.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {
        "to": "CSC",
        "content": "TDRA confirms alignment with the Council on the OpCo chatbot disclosure and restates its direction: account-lookup retrieval scope held at 'own_account'; no retrieval-scope, vendor or model change without documented change control, pre-deployment security testing against cross-account retrieval and prompt injection, and recorded human review; configuration, prompt-context, tool-invocation and human-review records preserved for TDRA and the Bureau; handler scripts must not confirm personal data to a caller; affected subscribers told the actions to be taken on a breach or misuse of their personal data. PDPL notification duties and timelines run to the Bureau, not TDRA, and the Council's advisory should carry the same split. The Council should obtain the operator-shareable indicator set from NOC."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S2-MSG30", "S2-MSG27", "S2-MSG17"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The Council has aligned its advisory and handler-script guidance with TDRA's direction and concurs that PDPL duties and timelines run to the Bureau (S2-MSG27, S2-MSG30).",
        "rule": "TDRA may notify other institutions, and the Consumer Protection Regulations give TDRA power over the handling of subscriber complaints and disputes, provision of information to subscribers, and usage of subscriber personal information.",
        "inference": "Confirming the direction and the TDRA/Bureau split in writing keeps the operator advisory and TDRA's regulatory position consistent."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000",
          "quote": "the handling of subscriber complaints and disputes, provision of information to subscribers, usage of subscriber personal information"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "request_audit",
      "params": {
        "of": "NOC",
        "topic": "the vendor update identifier and the retrieval-scope parameter change from 'own account' to 'all accounts'; the pre-deployment security testing performed against cross-account retrieval and prompt injection for the chatbot and the account-lookup tool; and the change-control and human-review records for the disable and the scoped re-enable"
      },
